# File: tests/unit/texture/test_jobs.py
# Generated from: specs/211-fix-texture-job-queue-duplicate-batch-outputs-orphaned-running-jobs-and-runner-log-location/requirements.md
Feature: The texture job queue keeps batch outputs, job states, and logs separate

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: A batch with a duplicate output name is rejected before anything runs
    Given a batch of requests named "burlap", "stone", and "Burlap"
    When it is submitted through generate --batch or generate_textures(requests=...)
    Then it is rejected with texture.invalid_request naming output 'burlap' and requests 0, 2
    And no job is queued, no worker runs, and no output folder is created

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: A job orphaned by a dead runner is marked failed and the queue continues
    Given a job left running by a runner whose PID is dead, and two queued jobs after it
    And a stale queue lock held by that dead PID
    When the next queue runner starts
    Then the orphaned job is failed with texture.runner_exited naming the dead PID
    And the two queued jobs succeed in submission order

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: The runner logs to its own file and each job log holds only its job
    Given two queued texture jobs
    When the queue runner runs both
    Then the runner's output is in runner.log under the jobs root, naming both jobs
    And each job's job.log names only that job
